"""Set Zulip presence and status text from the state of the desktop.

Runs as a systemd user service. Credentials come from ~/.zuliprc ([api] email,
key, site). As long as there is no key in it, the service only waits.

Presence:
  unlocked            -> visible + "active"
  locked >= N min     -> invisible (presence_enabled off)
  outside work hours  -> invisible, even when unlocked

Status (first matching line wins):
  sick / vacation by command        -> Sick [until DD.MM.] / On vacation until ...
  set by command (see below)        -> Break / Focusing until HH:MM
  all-day vacation event            -> On vacation until ...
  event running in the calendar     -> In a meeting until HH:MM
  unlocked, work hours, home net    -> Working from home
  unlocked, work hours, elsewhere   -> On the road
  unlocked, otherwise               -> empty
  locked >= N min, work hours       -> Away
  locked / service stop, otherwise  -> Off work, back at ...

Before suspend and hibernate (lid closed) the service delays sleep for a moment
and sets Away or Off work and invisible, because the machine cannot report
anything afterwards. Break/Focusing and vacation stay.

Settings: ~/.config/zulip-status/config.env (KEY=value), environment variables
of the same name win. ZULIP_STATUS_LANG=de|en selects the language of status
texts and messages (default: from the locale).

Optional calendar: ~/.config/zulip-status/kalender ([caldav] url, user,
password). Without it there is no meeting and no vacation status.

Optional dead man's switch: ~/.config/zulip-status/waechter ([waechter] url,
token). The service then reports to that server every round; see
docs/watchdog.md. Without the file nothing is sent anywhere but Zulip.

Break and focus are chosen by the user:
  zulip-status pause [MIN]   break; with MIN until that time, without until
                             the next unlock after a lock
  zulip-status fokus [MIN]   focusing; without MIN until end of work
  zulip-status krank [YYYY-MM-DD]   sick; with a date up to and including
                             that day, without until 'zulip-status auto'
  zulip-status urlaub YYYY-MM-DD    on vacation up to and including that day
  zulip-status auto          back to automatic

Sick and vacation also hold while the machine is off: sleep and service stop
leave the status in place, and so does the watchdog.

A status set by hand in Zulip stays. It is only cleared at the first unlock of
a new day, a status with the emoji "hurt" (sick) never.
"""
